{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgA8ufE3QzwqEBkRsZDoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: patterns passed with `--and` now get the same path-separator error as the main pattern. Before, `fd foo --and one/two` quietly returned no results.\n\n- **Change:** `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` in `src/main.rs` now checks every pattern, `--and` ones included. I moved the separator test into a small helper, `pattern_is_path`, so it can run on each one. The error message is the same, but it names the pattern that has the separator.\n- **Test:** I added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` to `tests/tests.rs`. It fails without the fix and passes with it, and the existing forward-slash tests still pass. **GATE PASS**. My first gate run failed only because I passed `cargo test` two name filters, which it doesn't accept.\n- **Not checked:** the Windows-only `\\` case for `--and` patterns, and the full test suite."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":35878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":408,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8995ca8d-3645-48c4-bb1c-da824953cb10","uuid":"15e70076-c6f7-41f2-9acf-70c118751d2f","timestamp":"2026-10-18T17:59:00.067Z","request_id":"req_011CgA8uf19SMcfakF9kMzHi"}
